{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And the fourth generation.</b> Rashi explained: go and count his generations — Judah, Perez, Hezron, and Caleb son of Hezron was among those who entered the land. And one should not object: but Hezron was among those who came to Egypt, and Caleb his son was among those who entered the land. This is what the verse says: <b>and the fourth generation</b> — for all who preceded the descent to Egypt, that is Judah; the fourth generation to him they shall return here, and they shall not remain in exile until the fifth generation. And one should not count the fourth generation from Jacob, for when he went down to Egypt, his days drew near to die. Another interpretation: <b>and the fourth generation shall return here</b> — at the fourth generation of the Amorites your children shall return from their exile here to inherit this land. Since one generation lives a hundred years, for four generations the four hundred years of servitude will be completed. And the verse did not say <b>fourth generation</b> except because such is the way of HaKadosh Barukh Hu to exact retribution from a person in his fourth generation, as it is written: ״upon the third and upon the fourth,״ meaning upon the third a little, and upon the fourth everything, to eradicate them from the world. And so we find regarding Jehu: ״your sons of the fourth shall sit upon the throne of Israel,״ and the fourth was killed and ceased from the world." "<b>For the iniquity of the Amorite is not yet complete.</b> And if you ask: why do I not bring them into the land immediately? The answer to the matter: <b>for the iniquity of the Amorite</b> who dwells in the land <b>is not yet complete</b> — <b>until here</b>, until the fourth generation." "<b>The iniquity of the Amorite.</b> It wrote <b>the Amorite</b> more than the other nations because Abraham was dwelling in the terebinths of Mamre the Amorite."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The abbreviation פרש״י is resolved as 'Rashi explained'; the familiar commentary is named here, rendered as it appears in the text."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:27.985622741Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}